The whole program reads one float with [38;5;10mscanf("%f", &x)[0m (with [38;5;10mx[0m pre-set to [38;5;10m0.f[0m) and prints the four bytes of its representation as [38;5;10m%02x[0m plus a newline. Since stderr is always empty and the exit status is always 0, the interesting behavior is entirely in what [38;5;10mscanf[0m stores — and specifically in what it [3mdoesn't[23m store.[0m[0m
